  "problem": {
    "id": "train-2177",
    "question": "Toby, the Alaskan Malamute, can pull a sled at a speed of 20 miles per hour if the sled is unloaded, but he pulls the same sled at a speed of 10 miles per hour if the sled is fully loaded.  If Toby takes a continuous 4-part journey, first pulling the loaded sled for 180 miles, then pulling the unloaded sled for 120 miles, then pulling the loaded sled 80 miles, and finally, pulling the unloaded sled another 140 miles, how many hours in total will Toby spend pulling the sled?",
    "gold": "39",
    "answer": "Pulling a loaded sled at 10 mph for 180 miles takes 180/10=<<180/10=18>>18 hours\nPulling an unloaded sled at 20 mph for 120 miles takes 120/20=<<120/20=6>>6 hours\nPulling a loaded sled at 10 mph for 80 miles takes 80/10=<<80/10=8>>8 hours\nPulling an unloaded sled at 20 mph for 140 miles takes 140/20=<<140/20=7>>7 hours\nIn total, Toby will have pulled the sled for 18+6+8+7=<<18+6+8+7=39>>39 hours\n#### 39"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total time Toby spends pulling the sled, we need to calculate the time spent on each part of the journey and then sum these times.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the time spent pulling the loaded sled for 180 miles. The speed of the loaded sled is 10 miles per hour. The time taken to pull the loaded sled is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{Time for loaded sled} = \\frac{180 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles per hour}} = 18 \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the time spent pulling the unloaded sled for 120 miles. The speed of the unloaded sled is 20 miles per hour. The time taken to pull the unloaded sled is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{Time for unloaded sled} = \\frac{120 \\text{ miles}}{20 \\text{ miles per hour}} = 6 \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nThen, let's calculate the time spent pulling the loaded sled for 80 miles. The speed of the loaded sled is 10 miles per hour. The time taken to pull the loaded sled is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{Time for loaded sled} = \\frac{80 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles per hour}} = 8 \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nFinally, let's calculate the time spent pulling the unloaded sled for 140 miles. The speed of the unloaded sled is 20 miles per hour. The time taken to pull the unloaded sled is given by:\n\\[\n\\text{Time for unloaded sled} = \\frac{140 \\text{ miles}}{20 \\text{ miles per hour}} = 7 \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nNow, we sum the times for all parts of the journey:\n\\[\n\\text{Total time} = 18 \\text{ hours} + 6 \\text{ hours} + 8 \\text{ hours} + 7 \\text{ hours} = 39 \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nThus, the total time Toby spends pulling the sled is \\(\\boxed{39}\\).",
